    {
      "id": "falsey-non-object-rules-bypass",
      "severity": "release-blocking",
      "summary": "The local and deployed /api/run adapters silently accept falsey non-object rules values as the default rule object.",
      "evidence": "POST bodies with rules=[], rules=\"\", rules=false, or rules=0 return HTTP 200 with a plausible default evaluation, while the same API correctly returns HTTP 400 `Rules must be an object.` for the truthy non-object rules=[1]. Source inspection shows `rules_override or {}` coerces the falsey invalid values before type validation.",
      "risk": "An invalid client payload can appear to succeed and produce decision output under rules the client did not validly supply, creating a fake-success and auditability risk.",
      "action": "Preserve the raw rules value through validation, default only for an explicitly supported omitted/null case, add regression tests for falsey non-object values, and run a new independent validation cycle."
    }
  ],
